    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27019" root="طلو and طلى" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُلْيَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُلَاةٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A portion, tuft,</i> or
<i>wisp, of wool, with which mangy camels are
daubed</i> [<i>with tar</i>]; also called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِبْذَةٌ</span>: whence the
saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا يُسَاوِى طُلْيَةً</span> [<i>It is not worth a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طلية</span>].
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَلْيَآءُ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طِلَآءٌ</span>, last
sentence.


